


Kafka — Always streaming, acts as a buffer:

API ──→ Kafka Topic (buffer) ──→ waiting...
         "jobs_raw" topic
         stores messages 24/7
         doesn't care if anyone is listening

Kafka just keeps collecting and holding the data like a queue — even when nothing is reading it.

Spark + Airflow — Only runs on schedule:

Airflow triggers (daily/@daily)
    → produce task   → pushes to Kafka
    → consume task   → pulls from Kafka buffer → saves to JSON
    → spark task     → cleans JSON → saves to CSV
    → load task      → CSV → Postgres

Spark only wakes up when Airflow tells it to.

Simple real world analogy:
Component	Analogy
API	News reporter writing articles
Kafka	Mailbox collecting articles 24/7
Airflow	Postman who comes once a day
Spark	Office worker who processes the mail
Postgres	Filing cabinet
Streamlit	Notice board everyone reads


    "Kafka acts as a real-time buffer, continuously collecting job data from the API. Every day Airflow triggers the pipeline — Spark processes the buffered data and loads it into Postgres for the dashboard."



